Ladybird answers navigator.storage.estimate() with a fixed 10 GiB
quota. Firefox’s QuotaManager::GetGroupLimitForLimit() caps a group
at min(a fifth of the temporary storage limit, 10 GB), which is the
10 GiB it reports on a large disk. Chrome’s QuotaSettings sets
per_storage_key_quota to a third of a pool that is 80% of the disk
(storage/browser/quota/quota_settings.cc, quota_features.cc), and
reported the same 10 GiB on the measured machine. WebKit computes an
origin quota from WebsiteDataStoreConfiguration’s origin quota ratio
of the volume, and Safari reported 82 GB. Ladybird uses the
disk-independent figure of the three.
